1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:02,960
If you own or follow SK hynix,

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:06,555
this is confusing: the company just posted record profits,

3
00:00:06,555 --> 00:00:08,910
yet the stock is still far below June.

4
00:00:09,710 --> 00:00:12,483
What the market watches isn't how big the profit is.

5
00:00:12,483 --> 00:00:13,710
It's how long it lasts.

6
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:16,541
I'll lay out the clues, one by one,

7
00:00:16,541 --> 00:00:18,050
in the next eight minutes.

8
00:00:18,850 --> 00:00:21,052
First, the numbers. On October 28,

9
00:00:21,052 --> 00:00:23,707
SK hynix reported third-quarter operating

10
00:00:23,707 --> 00:00:25,520
profit of 83.3 trillion won.

11
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:28,955
Today Samsung Electronics confirmed operating

12
00:00:28,955 --> 00:00:31,040
profit of 107.4 trillion won,

13
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:33,340
106.5 trillion of it from chips.

14
00:00:34,150 --> 00:00:34,522
Together,

15
00:00:34,522 --> 00:00:36,423
the two earned more than 190 trillion won from

16
00:00:36,423 --> 00:00:37,910
their core business in three months.

17
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,948
About 2 trillion won a day: roughly a thousand lottery jackpots,

18
00:00:41,948 --> 00:00:42,970
every single day.

19
00:00:43,770 --> 00:00:45,158
The stock reacted.

20
00:00:45,158 --> 00:00:48,012
SK hynix jumped 10.9% on results day,

21
00:00:48,012 --> 00:00:49,940
closing at 1,487,000 won.

22
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:52,047
But here's the odd part.

23
00:00:52,047 --> 00:00:55,226
Compared with the KOSPI peak on June 22,

24
00:00:55,226 --> 00:00:56,894
it's still 46% lower.

25
00:00:56,894 --> 00:00:59,040
Samsung is still 32% lower.

26
00:00:59,850 --> 00:01:01,714
Record profits, record payouts,

27
00:01:01,714 --> 00:01:04,540
and the stock is still near half its peak. Why?

28
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:08,540
First, where did this money come from?

29
00:01:09,330 --> 00:01:12,334
Here's SK hynix's quarter as a receipt.

30
00:01:12,334 --> 00:01:14,183
Sales of 104.6 trillion,

31
00:01:14,183 --> 00:01:17,032
minus 21.3 trillion to make and sell,

32
00:01:17,032 --> 00:01:18,650
leaves 83.3 trillion.

33
00:01:18,850 --> 00:01:21,480
Eighty won left on every hundred won of sales.

34
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:24,109
Like selling a fish-shaped pastry and spending

35
00:01:24,109 --> 00:01:25,310
only 20 won on flour.

36
00:01:26,110 --> 00:01:27,334
Versus a year earlier,

37
00:01:27,334 --> 00:01:30,560
sales are 4.3 times larger and operating profit 7.3 times.

38
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,483
Costs rose only 1.6 times.

39
00:01:32,483 --> 00:01:36,126
So this isn't money from selling four times more chips.

40
00:01:36,126 --> 00:01:37,120
Prices went up.

41
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:40,392
The company's earnings call gives the answer.

42
00:01:40,392 --> 00:01:43,193
It sold about 10% more DRAM than the prior quarter,

43
00:01:43,193 --> 00:01:45,390
but prices rose by the high 20s percent.

44
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:48,404
AI server builders are lining up for memory,

45
00:01:48,404 --> 00:01:50,890
and factories can't be built overnight.

46
00:01:51,690 --> 00:01:54,257
Quick detour: the memory SK hynix sells is like

47
00:01:54,257 --> 00:01:56,715
a workbench where a computer briefly lays out

48
00:01:56,715 --> 00:01:58,080
data while it calculates.

49
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:00,392
HBM is the high-performance kind,

50
00:02:00,392 --> 00:02:03,209
stacked in layers right next to the AI chip.

51
00:02:03,209 --> 00:02:05,642
Each AI chip carries several of these,

52
00:02:05,642 --> 00:02:08,010
so more AI servers means more memory.

53
00:02:08,810 --> 00:02:10,844
Samsung rode the same wind.

54
00:02:10,844 --> 00:02:14,311
Its chip division's operating profit rose 20%,

55
00:02:14,311 --> 00:02:17,400
from 89.2 trillion to 106.5 trillion won.

56
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,615
The first time its chip business alone topped

57
00:02:19,615 --> 00:02:20,780
100 trillion in a quarter.

58
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:21,729
In three months,

59
00:02:21,729 --> 00:02:23,882
chips alone earned nearly two and a half times

60
00:02:23,882 --> 00:02:26,597
the whole company's operating profit for all of last year,

61
00:02:26,597 --> 00:02:27,440
43.6 trillion won.

62
00:02:28,250 --> 00:02:28,405
So,

63
00:02:28,405 --> 00:02:30,838
part one: what the market still doesn't believe

64
00:02:30,838 --> 00:02:32,338
isn't the size of the profit.

65
00:02:32,338 --> 00:02:34,460
It's whether these prices hold into 2027.

66
00:02:34,650 --> 00:02:38,240
Money from selling more grows as factories grow.

67
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:41,980
Money from charging more shrinks when prices fall.

68
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:45,755
And high prices are pushing memory makers to build.

69
00:02:45,755 --> 00:02:49,750
SK hynix's first Yongin fab is set to open in early 2027.

70
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:54,484
Foreign investors sold a net 173 trillion won

71
00:02:54,484 --> 00:02:58,583
of these two stocks from January to October 12,

72
00:02:58,583 --> 00:03:01,810
87% of their total KOSPI net selling.

73
00:03:02,010 --> 00:03:03,994
Reasons vary, but by the numbers,

74
00:03:03,994 --> 00:03:07,660
the big money has leaned toward doubt rather than conviction.

75
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:10,965
On the other side were individual investors,

76
00:03:10,965 --> 00:03:13,527
who bought a net 22.8 trillion won of the two

77
00:03:13,527 --> 00:03:15,520
stocks from June 23 to results day.

78
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:19,441
A newspaper estimate from exchange data puts their paper losses,

79
00:03:19,441 --> 00:03:21,243
even after the two-day rebound,

80
00:03:21,243 --> 00:03:23,743
at about 2.8 trillion won. Record earnings,

81
00:03:23,743 --> 00:03:26,010
but many accounts are still in the red.

82
00:03:26,810 --> 00:03:28,541
But this worry isn't new.

83
00:03:28,541 --> 00:03:32,140
SK hynix has lived through this scene twice already.

84
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:36,410
Let's rewind to 2018.

85
00:03:37,210 --> 00:03:37,997
In Q3 2018,

86
00:03:37,997 --> 00:03:41,360
SK hynix kept 57 won of every 100 won of sales,

87
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:42,720
a record back then.

88
00:03:42,910 --> 00:03:45,212
But the stock turned first.

89
00:03:45,212 --> 00:03:48,025
From 95,300 won in May that year,

90
00:03:48,025 --> 00:03:51,690
it was down 39% to 57,700 by early January.

91
00:03:51,890 --> 00:03:56,020
The announcement that margins had fallen to 45% only came later,

92
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:57,310
on January 24, 2019.

93
00:03:58,120 --> 00:03:59,165
When prices fall,

94
00:03:59,165 --> 00:04:01,194
the same machine runs in reverse.

95
00:04:01,194 --> 00:04:03,408
In Q1 2023: 5 trillion won in sales,

96
00:04:03,408 --> 00:04:05,253
a 3.4 trillion operating loss.

97
00:04:05,253 --> 00:04:06,790
Lose 67 won on every 100.

98
00:04:06,990 --> 00:04:09,271
Factory and equipment costs stayed,

99
00:04:09,271 --> 00:04:10,770
while chip prices fell.

100
00:04:11,570 --> 00:04:16,685
Today's -46% may likewise be the market pricing in the worry early.

101
00:04:16,685 --> 00:04:19,204
So what's different now? For one,

102
00:04:19,204 --> 00:04:22,410
this quarter's margin rose from 76% in Q2.

103
00:04:22,610 --> 00:04:24,081
And this time there's a cushion,

104
00:04:24,081 --> 00:04:25,000
long-term contracts,

105
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,390
plus 100 trillion won to keep shareholders on board.

106
00:04:29,090 --> 00:04:31,421
SK hynix plans to return about 100 trillion won

107
00:04:31,421 --> 00:04:32,710
to shareholders this year.

108
00:04:33,510 --> 00:04:36,473
Over 30 trillion in cash dividends and over 60

109
00:04:36,473 --> 00:04:37,825
trillion in buybacks.

110
00:04:37,825 --> 00:04:41,690
The 40 trillion announced in August is already fully bought.

111
00:04:41,890 --> 00:04:46,893
Cancel bought-back shares and each remaining share owns more.

112
00:04:46,893 --> 00:04:49,190
Fewer slices, bigger slices.

113
00:04:49,990 --> 00:04:52,377
Samsung announced today a third-quarter

114
00:04:52,377 --> 00:04:54,458
dividend alone of 30 trillion won,

115
00:04:54,458 --> 00:04:55,560
4,601 won a share.

116
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:58,441
It plans to return 90 to 110 trillion this

117
00:04:58,441 --> 00:05:01,123
year; how to return the remaining 55 to 75

118
00:05:01,123 --> 00:05:04,570
trillion will be decided by the board in late January.

119
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:07,268
Record earnings, record payouts.

120
00:05:07,268 --> 00:05:09,923
But behind these numbers are three things the

121
00:05:09,923 --> 00:05:11,870
companies didn't fully spell out.

122
00:05:13,570 --> 00:05:16,460
Part two: what the companies didn't fully spell out.

123
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:18,437
First, the dividend.

124
00:05:18,437 --> 00:05:21,345
SK hynix pays 20,000 won a share for the quarter,

125
00:05:21,345 --> 00:05:23,660
but 10,000 of it is a special dividend.

126
00:05:23,860 --> 00:05:26,161
It shares out gains realized this year on Kioxia,

127
00:05:26,161 --> 00:05:28,979
the Japanese memory maker SK hynix invested in back in 2018.

128
00:05:28,979 --> 00:05:30,623
It's not money from selling memory,

129
00:05:30,623 --> 00:05:32,220
so it's hard to repeat every year.

130
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:35,030
Kioxia was originally Toshiba's memory business.

131
00:05:35,030 --> 00:05:37,586
SK hynix put in about 3.9 trillion won in 2018,

132
00:05:37,586 --> 00:05:41,120
and eight years later it's coming back as a shareholder dividend.

133
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:44,725
The bigger blank is long-term contracts.

134
00:05:44,725 --> 00:05:48,021
SK hynix says it has sold over half of its 2027

135
00:05:48,021 --> 00:05:50,826
and 2028 capacity to 14 major customers,

136
00:05:50,826 --> 00:05:52,720
usually on five-year deals.

137
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:55,450
The risk of suddenly not selling has clearly shrunk.

138
00:05:55,650 --> 00:05:56,503
But on price,

139
00:05:56,503 --> 00:05:58,932
it only said contracts reflect market

140
00:05:58,932 --> 00:06:02,082
conditions within a range agreed with customers.

141
00:06:02,082 --> 00:06:04,708
The floor and ceiling weren't disclosed.

142
00:06:04,708 --> 00:06:07,530
That's the first thing to check in January.

143
00:06:08,330 --> 00:06:10,707
Put simply, if market prices fall,

144
00:06:10,707 --> 00:06:13,784
contract prices fall too, within that range.

145
00:06:13,784 --> 00:06:17,280
The risk didn't disappear; the swing got narrower.

146
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:20,308
Samsung also said it's pursuing long-term

147
00:06:20,308 --> 00:06:23,550
contracts for 60 to 70% of its memory capacity.

148
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:26,396
The last blank is the calendar.

149
00:06:26,396 --> 00:06:30,730
Samsung's three-year return plan runs from 2024 through this year.

150
00:06:30,730 --> 00:06:32,700
There's no plan yet from 2027.

151
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:35,889
SK hynix says it'll keep buying back shares every quarter,

152
00:06:35,889 --> 00:06:37,590
but gave no figure for next year.

153
00:06:37,790 --> 00:06:40,695
So how is today's stock price filling in these blanks?

154
00:06:40,695 --> 00:06:42,900
Let's take out the calculator, just once.

155
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:45,465
When I look at companies like this,

156
00:06:45,465 --> 00:06:47,280
I put two calculations side by side.

157
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:50,775
Valued conservatively the Buffett and Graham way,

158
00:06:50,775 --> 00:06:54,675
on average profits over good and bad years with no growth,

159
00:06:54,675 --> 00:06:56,490
SK hynix comes to 29만 5천 원.

160
00:06:56,690 --> 00:07:00,077
If the last year's profit simply continues,

161
00:07:00,077 --> 00:07:01,494
you get 227만 5천 원.

162
00:07:01,494 --> 00:07:05,590
The Oct 29 장중 주가 is 153만 6천 원: somewhere in between.

163
00:07:05,790 --> 00:07:07,523
Neither is a price target.

164
00:07:07,523 --> 00:07:10,990
They show how widely this company's value can swing.

165
00:07:11,790 --> 00:07:14,725
Where it lands between the two depends on how

166
00:07:14,725 --> 00:07:16,290
long memory prices hold.

167
00:07:16,490 --> 00:07:18,864
The notebook where I log these two calculations

168
00:07:18,864 --> 00:07:20,884
for each company every day is ValueNote.

169
00:07:20,884 --> 00:07:22,450
The link is in the description.

170
00:07:24,150 --> 00:07:27,010
Part three: three numbers to check before January.

171
00:07:27,810 --> 00:07:29,867
One: DRAM contract prices,

172
00:07:29,867 --> 00:07:32,241
published at each month's end.

173
00:07:32,241 --> 00:07:37,305
TrendForce expects general DRAM to rise another 10 to 15% in Q4.

174
00:07:37,305 --> 00:07:41,420
Watch whether the increase shrinks to single digits.

175
00:07:41,620 --> 00:07:44,601
Two: SK hynix's Q4 results in late January.

176
00:07:44,601 --> 00:07:47,028
Does the 79.7% margin rise or fall,

177
00:07:47,028 --> 00:07:50,910
and is anything revealed about the contract price range?

178
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:53,038
Three: Samsung's board meeting,

179
00:07:53,038 --> 00:07:54,163
also late January,

180
00:07:54,163 --> 00:07:58,350
with the remaining 55 to 75 trillion and its return plan from 2027.

181
00:07:59,150 --> 00:08:00,946
You can try this on your own stocks.

182
00:08:00,946 --> 00:08:04,240
Write down a few years of sales and operating profit side by side.

183
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:07,972
If sales grew 1.5 times while profit grew 5 times,

184
00:08:07,972 --> 00:08:11,928
that company's profit depends more on price than volume.

185
00:08:11,928 --> 00:08:14,400
Don't value it on its best quarter.

186
00:08:15,210 --> 00:08:17,152
If you want more stories behind the numbers,

187
00:08:17,152 --> 00:08:19,050
please subscribe and turn on notifications.

188
00:08:19,250 --> 00:08:22,001
And check out our earlier video valuing SK

189
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:23,900
hynix the Warren Buffett way.

190
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:27,136
Which of the three numbers do you think moves first?

191
00:08:27,136 --> 00:08:29,180
Tell us in the comments. Thank you.
